  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Doubles are two pieces of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bara",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bara"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " wrapped around a generous spoonful of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "channa ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "channa"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The bara puffs when it hits hot oil and turns light and pillowy. The channa is a thick, spiced chickpea stew that should be almost dry, not saucy, so it holds in the bread without soaking through."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Traditional doubles are topped with cucumber chutney, tamarind sauce and pepper sauce. For this recipe the scotch bonnet gives heat directly in the channa. Eat them immediately after assembling while the bara is still warm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
